    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dōlĭŏlum</span></b> ,
		i, n.
		dim.
		dolium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a small cask.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				44, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 5, 40</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Nom. propr.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dōliŏla</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., <i>a
				place in Rome</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 157</span></i>
			Müll.; Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				69, 8</span></i> Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Doliola florum, <i>the
				calyx</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 13, 13, § 32</span></i>;
			cf. Schneid. on <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. p. 579</span></i>.</div>
